@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-dedicated-authority
Guest editor launch, approval, admission and renewal MUST require a current
stored login and fresh VM write permission.
Customer access additionally MUST require the exact VM owner. Generic web policy,
public visibility and peer identities MUST NOT authorize editor access.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] editor-refusal-classification
Missing, stale or revoked cookie/login identity MUST return authentication_required
so a fresh real sign-in can replace the personal host cookie. Current account,
profile, Customer owner or write denial MUST remain forbidden; missing route or
execution authority MUST remain unauthorized. Reauthentication MUST NOT revive
the old cookie or lease.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;concurrency] editor-account-execution-binding
Admission and renewal MUST retain the permanent GuestAccount UUID and UID,
gateway generation, host session, VM execution and
immutable image editor descriptor. Retired accounts and expired leases MUST NOT
renew. Email changes MUST NOT replace the account or invalidate its editor origin.
Lock order MUST remain service, host, VM, User, GuestAccount, credential,
lease. Initial launch allocation MUST use GuestAccounts' serialized allocator.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;observability] editor-redacted-durable-audit
Only credential hashes may persist. Audit transitions MUST commit atomically with
their mutation, outcome events MUST follow outer commit, and administrator reads
MUST be bounded and omit proofs, hashes, usernames, paths and request contents.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery;concurrency] editor-bounded-retention
Operational cleanup MUST delete at most 500 expired rows per transaction only
after seven days, with leases before unreferenced credentials and locked rows
skipped. Audit versions MUST remain independent. A full batch MUST schedule its
continuation atomically.
